cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Archaeopteryx, please cite it as below. A dedicated publication is in preparation; until it appears, cite the software and, where possible, the archived release DOI."
title: "Archaeopteryx"
abstract: >-
  Archaeopteryx is a desktop application for the visualization, annotation, and
  analysis of phylogenetic trees, built for publication-quality figures. It
  offers integrated taxonomy and sequence annotation, protein-domain
  architectures, calendar and geologic time axes, and WYSIWYG vector export.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Zmasek"
    given-names: "Christian M."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   # TODO: replace with the real ORCID
repository-code: "https://github.com/cmzmasek/Archaeopteryx"
url: "https://cmzmasek.github.io/archaeopteryx"
license: "GPL-3.0"
keywords:
  - phylogenetics
  - phylogenetic tree
  - tree visualization
  - phyloXML
  - bioinformatics
# When a release is archived on Zenodo, add its DOI here so GitHub's "Cite this
# repository" and the Zenodo record stay in sync:
# doi: "10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX"
